# Everything here is copied verbatim onto the device or consumed by the build,
# so it must never contain CRLF: a CR in a shell script breaks its shebang and
# stops 'then'/'fi' from being recognised as keywords, and CRs in the patches,
# feeds.conf and config.diff are just as fatal.
#
# text=auto + eol=lf makes git normalise every text file to LF in the
# repository and check it out as LF, so an edit made on Windows cannot
# reintroduce CRLF into a committed blob. Binary files are detected
# automatically and left untouched.
#
# Note: 'eol=lf' also means the working tree is LF, so a CRLF copy cannot be
# created by git in the first place - which is what let a plain edit silently
# turn custom.sh into a CRLF blob and break the build.
* text=auto eol=lf
